# Skill Expert Builder (v3.0.0)

**Creating expertise skills IS Test-Driven Development applied to knowledge curation.**

Creates skills at the **project level** (`<project-root>/.claude/skills/{topico}-expert/`), never global. Adapts output depth (flat/medium/deep) and style (expert/tutorial) to the topic.

Argument: $ARGUMENTS

**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** Skills follow RED-GREEN-REFACTOR. Skill content without research is worse than no skill.

## Iron Law

```
NO SKILL WITHOUT RESEARCH FIRST.
NO SKILL WITHOUT A FAILING BASELINE.
NO SKILL WITHOUT QUALITY GATES PASSED.
```

Write content before researching? Delete it. Restart.
Skip baseline? You don't know what gap you're filling.
Skip quality gates? You shipped untested process docs.

**No exceptions:**
- Not for "simple libraries I already know"
- Not for "the user is in a hurry"
- Not for "Context7 has it covered"
- Your training data may be stale. Research current sources anyway.

**Violating the letter of these rules is violating the spirit.**

## Process

```
Understand → Research → Baseline → Plan → Generate → Test → Deploy
   ↑                                          ↓
   └────────── loophole found ───────────────┘
```

1. **Understand** — Topic, stacks, mode, style
2. **Research** — Collect sources (mandatory, with fallback)
3. **Baseline (RED)** — What does an agent get wrong without this skill?
4. **Plan** — Structure proposal, user confirms
5. **Generate (GREEN)** — Build the skill
6. **Test (REFACTOR)** — Router test + quality gates
7. **Deploy** — Validate + report

## Inputs

- Topic (required)
- Stacks of interest (optional)
- Additional URLs (optional)
- Mode (optional): `flat` / `medium` / `deep` / `auto` (default)
- Style (optional): `expert` (default) / `tutorial`

## Modes

### `flat` — Single-file

For small/focused topics: single function, decorator, lib < 500 LOC, trivial SDK.

Output: one `SKILL.md` in `.claude/skills/{topico}-expert/` containing:
- Frontmatter
- Version header (builder + lib + date)
- Setup mínimo
- API/uso essencial
- 3-5 exemplos inline
- Troubleshooting (3-5 pontos)
- Princípios não-negociáveis
- Link to source

Target: 150-400 lines. Cap: 600. Exceeding cap → propose upgrade to `medium`.

### `medium` — Router + essential folders

For medium topics with 2-4 distinct areas.

```
{topico}-expert/
├── SKILL.md                    # router + core concepts inline
├── references/
│   ├── api-reference.md
│   └── troubleshooting.md
└── examples/
    ├── README.md
    └── 01-{n}-*.{ext}          # 3-7 curated
```

### `deep` — Full structure

For large/critical libs with multiple stack integrations, production patterns, breaking changes.

```
{topico}-expert/
├── SKILL.md                          # Router
├── references/
│   ├── core-concepts.md
│   ├── api-reference.md
│   ├── configuration.md
│   ├── integrations/{stack}.md       # one per relevant stack
│   ├── troubleshooting.md
│   └── changelog.md
├── examples/
│   ├── README.md
│   └── {NN-name}.{ext}               # 5-10 curated
├── recipes/{recipe-name}.md          # 5-10 production flows
└── snippets/
    ├── boilerplate.{ext}
    ├── env-template.md
    └── common-patterns.{ext}
```

Optional extra folders (Phase 4 proposes if content justifies):
`migration-guides/`, `benchmarks/`, `comparison/`, `security/`

### Auto-detection heuristic

| Signal | flat | medium | deep |
|---|---|---|---|
| Repo size | < 1k LOC | 1k-10k | > 10k |
| Docs sections | 1-2 | 3-8 | 10+ |
| Public API | < 10 | 10-30 | > 30 |
| Stack integrations | 0 | 1-3 | 4+ |
| Recent breaking changes | No | Maybe | Yes |

Heuristic guides, user confirms at Checkpoint 1.

## Style

### `expert` (default)
Skip onboarding. Direct: "Para X, faça Y. Comum errar Z." Assume context.

### `tutorial`
Include "Primeiros passos". Gradual complexity. More hand-holding in troubleshooting.

Auto-propose `tutorial` if: lib < 1 year old, small community, or user signals inexperience ("nunca usei"). Else `expert`.

## Description Rules — Triggers ONLY

**CRITICAL.** Description must contain triggers only, not workflow summaries:

```yaml
# BAD: Summarizes workflow — agent shortcuts the skill body
description: Expert in Traceloop — handles span instrumentation, exporter setup, langchain integration

# GOOD: Triggers only — agent reads the skill content
description: Use when instrumenting LLM applications with Traceloop, configuring exporters, or debugging missing spans
```

Why: empirical testing shows agents follow verbose descriptions instead of reading the SKILL.md content. Triggers-only forces the agent into the body.

Apply to BOTH this builder's output skills AND inside every recipe/reference frontmatter.

## Mandatory Research — Phase 2

**Before writing anything**, collect current sources. Stale skills are worse than no skill.

### Tier 1 — Structured tools (prefer)

| Tool | When |
|---|---|
| `mcp__context7` (`resolve-library-id` → `query-docs`) | Any indexed library |
| `web_search` | Discover URLs (docs, repos, examples) |
| `web_fetch` | Fetch identified URLs |

### Tier 2 — Shell fallback (ALWAYS available, first-class)

Use bash + curl when Tier 1 unavailable or returns junk. Not a desperate fallback — a real path.

**Source discovery:**
```bash
# DuckDuckGo HTML (no JS, returns direct links)
curl -sL --max-time 30 \
  "https://html.duckduckgo.com/html/?q=TOPIC+official+docs" \
  -A "Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36" \
  | grep -oE 'href="https?://[^"]+"' | head -20

# GitHub search (public, rate-limited but works)
curl -sL --max-time 30 \
  "https://api.github.com/search/repositories?q=TOPIC&sort=stars&order=desc" \
  | jq '.items[] | {name: .full_name, stars: .stargazers_count, url: .html_url}' \
  | head -20

# Repo README
curl -sL --max-time 30 \
  "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{org}/{repo}/main/README.md"
# Fallback if main 404:
curl -sL --max-time 30 \
  "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{org}/{repo}/master/README.md"
```

**Doc content (chain conversions):**
```bash
curl -sL --max-time 30 "https://docs.example.com/page" \
  -A "Mozilla/5.0" -o /tmp/page.html

pandoc /tmp/page.html -t markdown -o /tmp/page.md \
  || lynx -dump -nolist /tmp/page.html > /tmp/page.txt \
  || sed 's/<[^>]*>//g' /tmp/page.html > /tmp/page.txt
```

**GitHub examples:**
```bash
curl -sL --max-time 30 \
  "https://api.github.com/repos/{org}/{repo}/contents/examples" \
  | jq '.[] | {name: .name, download_url: .download_url}'

curl -sL --max-time 30 \
  "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{org}/{repo}/main/examples/foo.py" \
  -o /tmp/raw/foo.py

curl -sL --max-time 30 \
  "https://api.github.com/repos/{org}/{repo}/releases?per_page=10" \
  | jq '.[] | {tag: .tag_name, date: .published_at, body: .body}'
```

**Package registries:**
```bash
curl -sL --max-time 30 "https://pypi.org/pypi/{package}/json" \
  | jq '{version: .info.version, summary: .info.summary, home: .info.home_page}'

curl -sL --max-time 30 "https://registry.npmjs.org/{package}" \
  | jq '{version: ."dist-tags".latest, description: .description, repo: .repository.url}'
```

### Tier 3 — Last resort

If Tier 1 and Tier 2 both fail:
- Report **explicitly** which methods were tried and why each failed
- Ask user for URLs/content OR abort
- **Never** hallucinate. Missing source = no skill.

### Universal collection rules

- Realistic User-Agent (`-A "Mozilla/5.0 ..."`) — bare curl gets 403
- `-sL` (silent + follow redirects)
- `--max-time 30` on every curl
- Save to `.claude/skills/{topico}-expert/_raw/` before processing
- Detect junk: "Cloudflare", "Access Denied", "captcha" in HTML → try alternative
- 429: wait 5s, retry once; if fails, mark source unavailable
- Compute **quality score** per source (see below) before processing

### Quality score per source

```
quality_score = combine({
  density: useful_content / total_size,
  has_code_blocks: parseable ``` blocks present,
  has_structured_headings: # ## ### consistent,
  navigation_noise_ratio: menu/footer lines / total,
  encoding_issues: mojibake, unconverted HTML entities
})
```

Thresholds:
- `>= 0.7` — accept
- `0.4-0.7` — accept with warning, flag for review
- `< 0.4` — reject, try alternative

If ALL sources for a critical topic stay < 0.4 → escalate to Tier 3.

## Baseline — Phase 3 (RED)

Before generating, understand what an agent gets wrong WITHOUT this skill:

- Identify common mistakes, API misuse, outdated patterns from researched sources
- What gaps exist in default training knowledge?
- What patterns from examples contradict "obvious" approaches?
- What troubleshooting items appear repeatedly in issues/FAQs?

Document these. They become the troubleshooting and "common mistakes" content.

## Plan — Phase 4

Produce mode-specific plan:
- `flat`: SKILL.md outline (sections + bullets)
- `medium`: tree + 1 line justifying each file
- `deep`: full tree + 1 line per file + recipes list + stack integrations + extra folders if justified

Across all modes, identify:
- Core concepts (5-15)
- Subtopics by area
- Stack integrations (one entry per relevant stack)
- Patterns/anti-patterns observed in actual code
- Troubleshooting points (from real issues/FAQs)
- Production recipes

**CHECKPOINT 1**: present sources + collection methods + quality scores + complexity signals + proposed mode/style + detected stacks + failures. User confirms or adjusts.

**CHECKPOINT 2**: present plan with size estimates. User can add/remove items, change mode/style (replan), or request depth adjustments.

## Generate — Phase 5 (GREEN)

Sizes by mode:
- `flat`: SKILL.md 150-400 lines (cap 600)
- `medium`: SKILL.md 100-250 lines; references 100-400 lines
- `deep`: SKILL.md 100-300 lines (cap 500); references 200-500 lines (cap 800, split if exceeded); 5-10 examples; 5-10 recipes; ready-to-paste snippets

### Universal generation rules

1. **Frontmatter description = triggers only** (rule above)
2. **Version header** at top: builder version + lib version + date
3. **Non-negotiable principles**: 3-7 actionable rules (imperative, no vagueness like "use best practices")
4. **Curation, not copy**: paraphrase docs, condense; clean example boilerplate
5. **File justification** (medium/deep): each file has "Quando ler este arquivo" header
6. **Technical density**: code > prose, no fluff
7. **Language**: PT-BR content, English code comments
8. **Source attribution**: links to original docs at end of each reference
9. **Licenses**: GitHub example headers preserve license attribution
10. **Style respected**: expert skips onboarding; tutorial includes

### One excellent example beats five mediocre

For technique/integration skills, prefer one fully runnable, well-commented example over multiple half-baked variations. Multi-language examples dilute quality. Pick the dominant language of the topic.

### Dynamic upgrade/downgrade

If during generation the chosen mode is straining (flat overflowing 600 lines, deep producing near-empty files), pause and propose mode change instead of forcing a bad result.

## Test — Phase 6 (REFACTOR)

### Quality Gates (mandatory checklist)

Before Checkpoint 3, validate ALL. Any fail → fix and revalidate.

```
[ ] Description matches intent in < 200 chars
[ ] Description is TRIGGERS ONLY (no workflow summary)
[ ] Description starts with "Use when..." or equivalent actionable
[ ] SKILL.md has "Quando usar X" section with >= 3 testable rules
[ ] Every referenced file is pointed to by >= 1 when-to-use rule
[ ] No orphan files (referenced from nowhere)
[ ] Every example has header: context, what it demonstrates, min deps
[ ] Non-negotiable principles are actionable (imperatives, no vagueness)
[ ] Troubleshooting covers REAL errors from sources (not invented)
[ ] Lib version visible in first 10 lines of SKILL.md
[ ] Builder version in version header
[ ] YAML frontmatter parseable (name + description present)
[ ] Sizes respect mode caps
[ ] Source quality score average >= 0.6
```

### Router Test (medium/deep only)

Validate the router empirically before Checkpoint 3:

1. Generate 5-10 representative questions covering the topic (conceptual, debug, integration, production, edge cases)
2. For each, simulate: "If a user asked this, which file does the SKILL.md router point to?"
3. Validate:
   - Routing is deterministic (not "all files")
   - Pointed file actually covers the question
   - Distribution is balanced (no single file catching 90%)

If >= 2 questions fail routing:
- Refine SKILL.md (more specific rules)
- Or consolidate/split files
- Re-run test

Report Router Test results in Checkpoint 3.

### Rationalization Table

Skill must include a section anticipating common rationalizations for skipping it:

```markdown
| Excuse | Reality |
|--------|---------|
| "Vou ler depois" | Depois = nunca. Lê agora. |
| "Já sei o básico dessa lib" | A skill cobre o que você esqueceu. |
| "É só uma instrumentação rápida" | Quick patches viram dívida técnica. |
```

Tailor 3-5 entries to the specific topic.

**CHECKPOINT 3**: present:
- Final tree (or single file if flat)
- Sizes
- Full SKILL.md preview
- Preview of 1 example + (if applicable) 1 reference + 1 recipe
- Quality Gates checklist (✓/✗)
- Router Test results (if medium/deep)

User confirms or requests adjustments.

## Deploy — Phase 7

- Validate parseable frontmatter
- Medium/deep: generate `INDEX.md` with file map + searchable tags
- Clean `_raw/`
- Final report:
  - Path
  - Mode + style
  - Builder version + lib version
  - File count / total lines
  - Collection methods + average quality scores
  - Quality Gates results
  - Router Test results
  - Git command: `git add .claude/skills/{topico}-expert`

## Refresh vs Rebuild Policy

When skill already exists in `.claude/skills/{topico}-expert/`, offer:

### `refresh` — Surgical update preserving customizations

**Always regenerate** (sourced from docs, no user value):
- `references/api-reference.md`
- `references/core-concepts.md`
- `references/changelog.md`
- `references/configuration.md`
- `references/integrations/{stack}.md`
- Examples with `# Source: official-repo` header

**Always preserve** (user-created/customized):
- `recipes/*.md`
- `snippets/*.md`
- Files with `# Custom: true` header (convention)
- `INDEX.md` if edited (detect via diff)

**Smart merge**:
- `references/troubleshooting.md` — preserve sections marked `<!-- USER ADDITIONS -->`
- `SKILL.md` — preserve "Custom Rules" section if exists

Before refresh:
1. Full backup to `.claude/skills/.backups/{topico}-expert-{timestamp}/`
2. Apply rules
3. Report exactly what was updated, preserved, merged

### `rebuild` — Full overwrite

Deletes everything (after backup) and regenerates. Use when skill is severely outdated or generated by very old builder.

### `migrate` — Builder version upgrade

If existing skill was generated by `< v3.0.0`:
- Read current structure
- Identify gaps vs v3.0.0 (missing version headers, quality gates, etc)
- Regenerate ONLY missing/divergent parts
- More conservative than refresh — touches only what changed between builder versions

### `abort`

Cancel.

## Red Flags — STOP and Restart

- Writing skill content before researching current sources
- Copying API patterns from training data without verification
- Description summarizes workflow instead of triggers
- Skipping baseline analysis (no understanding of what's wrong without skill)
- Multiple mediocre examples instead of one excellent
- Skipping Quality Gates "because it's a simple skill"
- Skipping Router Test "because medium/deep is overkill"
- "Já conheço essa lib o suficiente" — research anyway
- "Pesquisa demoraria muito" — stale skills cost more
- "É só uma referência simples" — references have gaps. Validate retrieval.

**All of these mean: Stop. Research. Restart the phase.**

## Anti-Patterns

| Anti-pattern | Why bad | Do instead |
|---|---|---|
| Narrative ("Encontramos que...") | Not reusable | State the pattern directly |
| Multi-language examples | Dilutes quality | One excellent example |
| Code inside flowcharts | Can't copy-paste | Use markdown code blocks |
| Workflow in description | Agent shortcuts skill | Triggers only |
| Skipping Tier 2 fallback | Builder fails without MCP | curl is first-class |
| Hallucinating because source quality < 0.4 | Wrong > missing | Escalate to Tier 3 |
| Orphan files in deep mode | Tokens wasted | Every file pointed to from SKILL.md |
| Generic principles ("seja consistente") | Not actionable | Imperatives ("sempre rodar `init` antes de import de openai") |
| Batch-creating skills | Untested = broken | One skill, fully tested, then next |

## Invocation Examples

- `"create a skill expert for traceloop"` — auto-detect everything
- `"create a flat skill for python pathlib"` — force flat
- `"deep expert of langgraph for python + fastapi"` — force deep + stacks
- `"tutorial skill for mem0, never used it"` — force tutorial style
- `"refresh traceloop-expert"` — refresh policy
- `"migrate langgraph-expert to v3"` — migrate command

## Final Output

1. Skill in `.claude/skills/{topico}-expert/` (mode + style applied)
2. INDEX.md (medium/deep)
3. Backup (refresh/rebuild/migrate)
4. Report:
   - Path
   - Mode + style
   - Builder + lib versions
   - Stats (files, lines)
   - Collection methods + quality scores
   - Quality Gates checklist
   - Router Test results (if applicable)
   - Git command
